  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADB Agricultural Programme (CASP 2) 2012 - 2018 - ADB Core Agric. Supp. Prog. 2 (CASP 2)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ADB Jordbruksprogram CASP 2 2012 - 2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till Asian Development Bank och deras Greater Mekong Subregion   (GMS) Program inom vilket detta st&#xf6;d g&#xe5;r till ADBs Working Group for  Agriculture (WGA) och det program som WGA koordinerar &quot;Core           Agricultural Support Programme (CASP)&quot;. St&#xf6;d fokuserar p&#xe5; omr&#xe5;dena    regional handel med jordbruksprodukter samt klimats&#xe4;kring av          matproduktion.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the Asian Development Bank and the Greater Mekong         Sub-region (GMS) Program under which this aid goes to the ADBs        Working Group for Agriculture (WGA) and the program that the WGA      coordinates &quot;Core Agricultural Support Programme (CASP)&quot;. Support     focuses on the areas of regional trade in agricultural products as    well as climate adaptation of food production.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Core Agriculture Support Program, Phase II (CASP 2), 2011-2020, brings together the six countries of the GMS &#x2013; Cambodia, Guangxi and Yunnan in the People&#x2019;s Republic of China, the Lao PDR, Myanmar, Thailand, and Viet Nam &#x2013; in common purpose to respond to these changes while safeguarding the natural ecosystems that underpin agricultural production in the region.
The overall vision of CASP 2 is for the GMS to be recognized as the leading producer of safe food, using climate-friendly agricultural practices and integrated into global markets through regional economic corridors. This vision aligns with and supports the two pillars of the ASEAN Economic Community blueprint &#x2013; the creation of a single market and production base for food, agriculture, forestry, and integration of the region into the global economy.
The broad strategy of CASP 2 aims to increase subregional agricultural competitiveness and agribusiness investment through modernized trading system that provides links to regional and global markets. The foundation of the strategy includes agricultural research and technology that emphasizes climate-friendly agricultural development, private-sector involvement to ensure sustainability, and institutional mechanisms to enhance regional cooperation with incentives to achieve the vision.</narrative>
  </description>
